    <item>
      <title>Meta's New Muse Wonder AI Model; LVMH Slumps After China Backlash</title>
      <link>https://www.bloomberg.com/news/videos/2026-10-13/daybreak-europe-10-13-2026-video</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">6fc035a8b3aebce0139010e9</guid>
      <pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 06:48:28 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>Bloomberg Daybreak Europe is your essential morning viewing to stay ahead. Live from Brussels, we set the agenda for your day, catching you up with overnight markets news from the US and Asia. And we'll tell you what matters for investors in Europe, giving you insight before trading begins.

On today's show, global stock losses deepened on renewed concerns about the AI trade. Korea's Kospi slid 7% after the Broadcom CEO Hock Tan compared AI investors to gamblers in a casino.

LVMH reported a 5% fall in sales in its biggest division, the fashion and leather goods unit, as worsening economic conditions and a consumer backlash in China hit its key Louis Vuitton brand.

And the Indian Prime Minister Narendra Modi says the world is undergoing a "big transformation" where new technology has the power to create opportunities for millions of people. He was speaking in his keynote address at the Bloomberg New Economy Forum in New Delhi. (Source: Bloomberg)</description>
