      <description>India is in the middle of a massive exercise to revise its electoral rolls by removing dead, duplicate and ineligible voters. But concerns that eligible voters could also be struck off the rolls — potentially affecting election outcomes — have turned the Special Intensive Revision, or SIR, into a politically charged controversy.</description>
